      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Several of the most popular public-facing event groups dedicate a lot of effort, and deal with a lot of friction and confrontation when trying to implement manual performance limit enforcement. Much in the same way groups were added in the first place to fit the needs of the community, I believe expanding the capabilities for those groups to control, moderate, and regulate their own instances is a step towards a safer experience for group staff, and a more seamless experience for attendees; especially those who need the lower performance ratings to enjoy the game.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
