      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Giving an option to limit joining the instance based on the avatar performance rank shouldn't be a big issue, given it would be enforced for every user. And it could be toggled/edited like current item/drone/print toggles in instance settings.\n\nI'm guessing the \"issue\" why this is not implemented yet is whitelisting certain users within the instance to be allowed to bypass the requirement. \n\nNothing here is impossible to implement and by implementing this will certainly lift a massive weight of the shoulders of event hosts, not to mention client and server performance impact.\n\nIn my opinion, this should go to the top of the priority list.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
